{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>By the mirrors of the women who assembled.</b> Of the root ראיה, seeing. Its meaning: it was placed between the Tent of Meeting and the altar, drawn somewhat toward the north, so that the assembling women would see it and be reminded that from there the suspected adulteresses are given to drink, as it is written in the portion of the suspected adulteress, 'holy water in an earthen vessel' — and they translate it: the water of the laver, in a vessel of clay. And according to Rashi's interpretation, <b>במראת הצבאת</b> is like ממראות, the bet in place of mem — as in 'and that which remains of the meat and of the bread.'" "<b>Who assembled at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting.</b> To pray, and to hear the praises and hymns of the Holy One, blessed be He, from the mouths of the priests and the Levites."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The text cites Rashi by the standard abbreviation; the instruction to avoid names he did not write applies to unnamed sources, but here פרש״י is explicitly written in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:09.577272049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}